tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.experiencePresets=Select a preset to fill this form immediately. Aging: Simplified turns aging off; Easier freezes adults at their prime; Full Experience and Hardcore use full aging, but only Hardcore enables old-age death. All presets set animal progression to owner-online grace then decay (72h grace, 1× offline rate) and use only the higher hunger/thirst damage value. Hardcore also disables revives and recall teleportation, and sets starvation damage to 10% max health/minute and dehydration damage to 15% max health/minute.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.loadPreset=Selecting a preset fills this form immediately. Apply saves it.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.presetScope=Presets set aging, animal progression, revives, recall teleportation, and needs damage. Resource search mode, ownership, population, claims, and telemetry stay unchanged. Apply saves changes.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.recallSection=Controls whether recall and return-home commands may teleport companions when normal movement cannot reach them.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.recallTeleporting=When disabled, recall and return-home commands will not teleport unloaded or distant companions. Use Locate to see their last recorded location.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.companionSystems=High-level toggles for the main companion gameplay systems that Tamework can run.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.needsEnabled=Turns hunger and thirst simulation on or off for companions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.happinessEnabled=Turns happiness tracking on or off for companions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.passiveBreedingEnabled=Allows companions to breed on their own when breeding conditions are met.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.breedingRequiresHappiness=Requires companions to satisfy happiness rules before passive breeding can happen.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.levelingEnabled=Allows companions to gain XP, level up, and apply level-based stat growth.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.talentsEnabled=Allows companion talent points, talent spending, and purchased passive talent effects.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.breedingGenderEnabled=Turns companion gender assignment and gender-aware breeding checks on or off.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.traitsEnabled=Turns trait generation and trait-based companion effects on or off.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.needsSection=Controls hunger and thirst damage, offline decay behavior, and how needs-based damage is calculated.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.needsResourceMode=Controls how hungry or thirsty companions reach food and water. Accurate uses path checks and movement. Auto Fast keeps accurate behavior until needs search/path pressure is high. Always Fast consumes directly from valid nearby sources without movement. Default when no choice is saved: Auto Fast.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.needsDamageEnabled=Applies damage when hunger or thirst reaches the configured minimum threshold.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.needsTickPolicy=Chooses when needs are allowed to tick, such as after an owner's offline grace period or whenever any player keeps the area loaded.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.ownerOfflineGraceHours=How many hours an owner can stay offline before needs begin decaying under the owner-online grace policy.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.ownerOfflineDecayMultiplier=Multiplier applied to needs decay after the owner has been offline longer than the grace period.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.needsDamageModel=Chooses how starvation or dehydration damage is calculated once a need bottoms out.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.dualNeedRule=Chooses whether low hunger and low thirst use only the higher damage amount or add both together.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.starvationDamagePerMinute=Damage applied per minute when hunger is depleted and the current damage model uses starvation damage.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.dehydrationDamagePerMinute=Damage applied per minute when thirst is depleted and the current damage model uses dehydration damage.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.needsDamageLethal=When enabled, needs damage can kill companions. When disabled, it stops at 1 health.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.ownership=Controls owner-only protections, capture behavior, and general ownership checks for companions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.damageProtection=Protection rules that apply to owned companions during damage events.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.blockOwnerDamage=Prevents the owner from damaging their own owned companions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.blockAllDamageIfOwned=Prevents all player-sourced damage against owned companions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.invulnerableIfOwned=Makes owned companions ignore all damage, not just player damage.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.capture=Rules for owner requirements during capture and spawn flows.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.captureRequiresOwner=Requires a companion to already have an owner before it can be captured with supported Tamework items.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.spawnRequiresOwner=Requires an owner assignment before a companion can be spawned from supported Tamework items.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.captureClearsOwner=Removes ownership when a companion is captured.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.spawnSetsOwner=Assigns the spawning player as owner when the companion is spawned.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.captureTrade=If both capture clears owner and spawn sets owner are enabled, captured companions can be transferred between players.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.general=Owner requirement rules for common companion interactions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.interactionRequiresOwner=Restricts supported companion interactions so only the owner can use them.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.linkingRequiresOwner=Restricts command-item linking so only the owner can link a companion.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.reviveSystem=Controls whether dead owned companions can use Tamework's revive flow.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.reviveSystemEnabled=Allows supported Tamework revive and respawn behavior for owned companions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.population=Controls Tamework's per-player cap for canonical owned companion profiles, including active, unloaded, captured, cooped, dead, lost, restoring, and dormant companions.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.populationLimit=Maximum owned companions per player before Tamework blocks new ownership, transfer, restore, or acquisition. Existing over-cap companions are preserved.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.populationScope=Counts owned companions separately by their retained ownership world or across the entire universe.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.simpleClaims=Controls provider-neutral claim admission limits plus the independent SimpleClaims tamed-target damage policy.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.simpleClaimsEnabled=Master switch for claim integration. Population also needs a selected provider and relevant cap or breeding claim rule; damage also needs the tamed-damage toggle.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.claimLimitChunk=Maximum physically active or durably unloaded owned companions admitted to one claim chunk. Natural movement is not blocked.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.claimLimitTotal=Maximum physically active or durably unloaded owned companions admitted across the entire claim. Stored, cooped, dead, and lost companions do not occupy it.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.breedingRequiresClaim=Requires breeding destinations to be claimed through the selected provider, even when no positive claim cap is configured.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.simpleClaimsProtect=Uses SimpleClaims native full-world, admin, member-permission, player/party ally, and outsider rules for eligible live tamed targets. Integration errors fail open.
tamework.ui.settings.tooltip.telemetrySection=Telemetry consent is managed by the shared Beacon command.

